<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine sees 37-38 mln T grain crop - news agency.</title>
<headline>Ukraine sees 37-38 mln T grain crop - news agency.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine expects a net grain harvest of 37 to 38 million tonnes this year against 25.4 million tonnes in 1996, the state news agency DINAU/Ukrinform said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;According to forecasts, the total grain and corn harvest is expected to be 37 to 38 million tonnes,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The Agriculture Ministry last month revised its grain output forecast up to 37 million tonnes from 35 million.</p>
<p>DINAU/Ukrinform said it was quoting newly-appointed Agriculture Minister Yuri Karasyk and other officials.</p>
<p>It said the government had given farms until August 15 to complete the harvest, which has been slowed due to recent heavy rains.</p>
<p>--Kiev Newsroom +380 44 244-9150</p>
</text>
